    "explanation": "Both of you broadly agree on what happened, and so does the platform's record; the question is what the policy does with it. The driver says he went PIE then CTE and took the Braddell exit around a small jam near Toa Payoh, 'maybe one or two km more'. The rider says he was taken through unfamiliar back roads and overcharged. The trip record and the GPS trace both put the trip at 16.5 km against a booked optimal route of 14.2 km - 2.3 km more. Under POL-RD-01 the GPS trace figure governs the distance, and here it matches the trip record exactly (16.5 km both), so there is no distance dispute to resolve.\n\nThat 2.3 km is not enough to make the extra charge refundable. POL-RD-01 establishes a route deviation only where the excess is BOTH more than 20% of the optimal distance AND more than 0.8 km in absolute terms, and both tests must pass. The absolute test passes (2.3 km > 0.8 km), but the percentage test does not: 2.3 km is 16.2% of 14.2 km, under the 20% line. No deviation is therefore established, so the recomputation in POL-RD-02 - which, if it ran, would give charged_total SGD 24.74 less a recomputed fare of SGD 21.13, about SGD 3.65 - does not run at all. The charge of SGD 24.74 stands, payment_status stays CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd stays 0.00. Under POL-GEN-03 this is NO_ACTION on a rider-filed dispute: the present state is left as it is, and nothing is refunded to the rider and nothing is owed to the driver.\n\nI have checked every route by which the rider could still recover, and none is open. There is no traffic advisory covering this trip (EV-ADVIS-00301-01 is MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), so POL-RD-03 cannot be run either to excuse any of the extra distance or to build an adjusted optimal; that absence is neutral here, because the case fails on the distance figures themselves, and the driver's 'there was a jam' explanation carries no weight under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-13. The in-app chat for the trip is empty (0 messages), so there was no rider instruction that could have made any part of the distance rider-caused (POL-RD-04). Neither endpoint was amended and the amended-optimal fields are null (POL-RD-05), and the vehicle was RYDE_X, not a pooled trip (POL-RD-12). The fare carries no ERP gantry lines and no airport surcharge, so there is no standalone billing-integrity correction under POL-RD-09(4). The rider's profile does not trigger the extra-corroboration overlay in POL-RD-08, but that makes no difference, because the threshold itself is not met.\n\nOn the rider's request that the driver be flagged: POL-RD-06 comes into play only on a MATERIAL deviation (over 50% or 8.0 km), which this 16.2% / 2.3 km trip does not approach, and this driver's record shows 0 deviation flags over 260 completed trips, so no repeat pattern is established and no driver-conduct referral is available.\n\nFor completeness of the figures: the record shows SGD 24.74 actually charged, not the SGD 25.63 mentioned by the rider; the disputed SGD 3.50 is not refunded and no driver compensation is payable. The monetary effect of this ruling is nil, below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so there is nothing to hold or release. This ruling was made without human review; either party may appeal it under POL-GEN-04."
