    "explanation": "The charge stands. This dispute is decided on the distance figures alone, and they do not clear the gate.\n\nTo the rider: You say the driver took an unnecessarily long way. The governing measurement is the platform's GPS trace (EV-GPS-00301), which is complete and unimpaired — 167 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0 seconds, so it satisfies none of the impairment limbs in POL-RD-07(a) to (c). It records 16.5 km driven against the booked optimal route of 14.2 km (EV-TRIP-00301), an excess of 2.3 km. Under POL-RD-01 a route deviation is established only if the excess is greater than 20% of the optimal distance AND greater than 0.8 km absolute. The absolute limb is met (2.3 km), but the percentage limb is not: 20% of 14.2 km is 2.84 km, and 2.3 km is only 16.2% of the optimal. Both limbs must pass, so no deviation is established however the trip felt, and the fare arithmetic in POL-RD-02 does not run. No refund is due.\n\nThe fare itself is clean. Charged_total was SGD 24.74; the recomputed figure of SGD 21.13 in EV-FARE-00301 is illustrative only and is not money the policy owes where the POL-RD-01 gate fails. There are no ERP gantries, no airport surcharge (the trip neither starts nor ends at an airport) and no phantom charge lines, so no billing-integrity correction under POL-RD-09(4) arises. (Your recollection of $25.63 does not match the ledger's $24.74; the ledger figure is the one recorded.)\n\nYour request to flag the driver is also declined. The excess is not a MATERIAL deviation (far below 50% of optimal and 8.0 km), so the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is not even engaged; and if it were, driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 260 completed trips in 90 days (EV-DPROF-00301), so no repeat pattern and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral is available. That ends the flagging request.\n\nTo the driver: Your explanation of a jam near Toa Payoh carries no weight. No traffic advisory covers this trip window — EV-ADVIS-00301-01 is MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and your assertion discharges no burden under POL-RD-08. It does not, however, escalate this case: no party invoked that absent advisory's identifier as the basis of an exoneration, so under POL-RD-13(1) this is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, and POL-RD-10(5) is not triggered. The outcome rests on the trace and the optimal-route figure regardless, so nothing turns on it.\n\nBoth figures that decide this case — the trace distance and the optimal distance — are carried by artifacts of full weight (EV-GPS-00301 and EV-TRIP-00301, both 1.0), so confidence is high. The monetary effect is nil, below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold, and there is no referral under any clause. This ruling is provisional and may be appealed once under POL-GEN-04."
